            <abstract>
                <p>
                    <foreign xml:lang="gez">Tawāqǝso ba-hāymānot</foreign> is a work on a disputation between a Christian priest and two Muslim jurists. 
                    It was translated into Gǝʿǝz by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9683Urbino">Giusto da Urbino</persName> in <date when="1952">1852</date> from French. The title of the original work is <foreign xml:lang="fr">Soirées de Carthage, ou Dialogues entre un prêtre catholique, un muphti et un cadi par l'abbé Bourgade</foreign>. The work is attested in 
                    <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BAVet165">Vatican City, Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Aeth. 165</ref>.
                    An Amharic version of the same work is <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7754Disputation">Maṣḥafa takāhǝdo ba-hāymānot</ref>.
                </p>
            </abstract>
